# ============================================================
# BookApi — HTTP Test File
# How to use in VS Code:
#   1. Install the "REST Client" extension (by Huachao Mao)
#   2. Click "Send Request" above any request to run it
#   3. Run them IN ORDER — register first, then login, then books
# ============================================================

# The base address of our API — change the port if dotnet run uses a different one
@host = http://localhost:5243

# After you run the Login request, copy the token value from the response
# and paste it below (replace the placeholder text)
@token = PASTE_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE


### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### STEP 1 — Register a new user
### Expected response: 200 OK "User registered successfully."
### ─────────────────────────────────────────
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "password123"
}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### STEP 2 — Login with that user
### Expected response: 200 OK { "token": "eyJhbG..." }
### Copy the token value and paste it into @token above
### ─────────────────────────────────────────
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "password123"
}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### STEP 3 — Try accessing books WITHOUT a token
### Expected response: 401 Unauthorized  ← proves [Authorize] works
### ─────────────────────────────────────────
GET {{host}}/api/books


### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### STEP 4 — Create a book (requires token)
### Expected response: 201 Created — returns the new book with its Id
### ─────────────────────────────────────────
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Dune",
  "author": "Frank Herbert",
  "publicationDate": "1965-08-01"
}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### STEP 5 — Get all books (requires token)
### Expected response: 200 OK — array containing the book we just created
### ─────────────────────────────────────────
GET {{host}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### STEP 6 — Update the book (change Id if yours is different)
### Expected response: 200 OK — returns the updated book
### ─────────────────────────────────────────
PUT {{host}}/api/books/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Dune (Updated)",
  "author": "Frank Herbert",
  "publicationDate": "1965-08-01"
}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### STEP 7 — Create a quote (requires token)
### Expected response: 201 Created
### ─────────────────────────────────────────
POST {{host}}/api/quotes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "text": "The mystery of life is not a problem to be solved but a reality to be experienced."
}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### STEP 8 — Get all quotes (requires token)
### Expected response: 200 OK — array with the quote above
### ─────────────────────────────────────────
GET {{host}}/api/quotes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────
### STEP 9 — Delete the book (requires token)
### Expected response: 204 No Content
### ─────────────────────────────────────────
DELETE {{host}}/api/books/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
